        conceptEn: "A flaky test sometimes fails without a code change because of races, time, test order, external networking, or shared data. Capture logs and failure conditions, isolate data and dependencies, and control the clock where needed. Instead of a fixed sleep, wait for the specific condition with a bounded timeout: finding an element in the DOM does not by itself establish visibility. For random tests, record the seed and counterexample; fast-check also reports a path to replay shrinking. A seed does not eliminate races or external-state dependencies. A unit test can substitute a payment API, while the real integration is checked separately in a safe test environment. A rerun can aid diagnosis but does not fix the cause.",
